# Effective collision strengths for the he_top_lines_coll.dat transitions (He I, he_top levels).
# Source: CHIANTI he_1 (Sawey & Berrington 1993, ADNDT 55, 81; Bray et al. 2000, A&AS 146, 481),
# Burgess & Tully (1992) fits.  J components are summed into he_top terms and re-sampled at the
# 13 BT nodes of the listed type and C, with the reduced temperature defined by the he_top
# transition energy.  Accuracy of each record (as Sirocco evaluates it) against the CHIANTI sum:
# 1s2 1S - 1s2s 3S     he_top 1-2  CHIANTI 1-2             BT type 3 C=0.06  max |dUps/Ups| (1e3-1e6 K) = 1.1%
# 1s2s 3S - 1s2s 1S    he_top 2-3  CHIANTI 2-3             BT type 2 C=1.6   max |dUps/Ups| (1e3-1e6 K) = 1.2%
# 1s2s 3S - 1s2p 1P    he_top 2-5  CHIANTI 2-7             BT type 3 C=1.1   max |dUps/Ups| (1e3-1e6 K) = 0.0%
# 1s2s 1S - 1s2p 3P    he_top 3-4  CHIANTI 3-4+3-5+3-6     BT type 2 C=5     max |dUps/Ups| (1e3-1e6 K) = 2.6%
# 1s2p 3P - 1s2p 1P    he_top 4-5  CHIANTI 4-7+5-7+6-7     BT type 2 C=6.7   max |dUps/Ups| (1e3-1e6 K) = 1.3%
